WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.067 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-How are you?

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:03.069 line:92%
-I am exhilarated to be here

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:03.770 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I thank you very much.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:07.073
-Right. Exhausted little bit
from the last couple weeks

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.008 line:92%
But it ended with a blast.

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:10.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it was amazing match
in the final.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.144 line:92%
And Serena got to the final.

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:12.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that was good.
-It was a great U.S. Open.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.414
It's obviously very exciting
to have tennis in New York City.

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
You mentioned both exhilaratio
and exhaustion.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:19.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I feel like that must been
what it felt like

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:21.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
on Sunday night
with a five-hour men's final

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were in the booth
with your brother, Patrick

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Do you ever --

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:27.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you feel an exhaustion
sitting in on yourself,

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
or did you feel the excitement
of the match?

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:30.497 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I have --

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:33.700
If you get exhausted watchin
two guys battle like that,

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's something wrong
with you.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're a little
sick in the head.

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:39.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And for us, you know, the men

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:41.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
to go at it like that,
I mean, I've played matches --

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:44.411 size:84% position:42%
a couple matches longer
than that, so I get it,

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:45.645 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and I respect it.

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.580 line:92%
So I was having a great time

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.649
We know there's a tie breaker in
the fifth set.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it could only go
another 20, 30 minutes.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:53.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
What's another half-hour?
So it was -- It ended great.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:56.589
-And what -- Do you feel lik
the energy in New York Cit

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a match like that is
different than any other place

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:01.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you have a major final
like this?

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.562 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Without question.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:03.863 line:92%
Did anyone see the final?

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.732 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:09.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was lucky enough to be par
of five U.S. Open finals.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:14.007
And that may have been one o
the loudest, if not the loudest,

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:16.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
when this, you know, Medvedev,
this Russian guy,

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
came back and took it
to a fifth set.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:21.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it inspires the players
obviously.

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:22.782 line:92%
It's absolutely incredible

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
We need a shot in the arm
for our sport.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.352 line:92%
We -- The women are doing well

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light applause ]
But, you know, the men, the --

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:30.857 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:34.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do have four daughters
and two boys.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I -- You know,
how much it means

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:40.867
now that the playing field
is more level in women's gam

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
in our sport
than any other sport.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:45.872
You know, you talked about -
I've heard that soccer joke.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That was just --

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
the previous --
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Basketball.
There's no football.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.780
You know, they're getting paid
1/20th, 1/50th what the men do

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
In tennis, exactly the same.
Equal prize money.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:59.919 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-What -- if you were --

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.221 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Very -- Absolutely true.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:03.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's exactly as exciting
going into the finals.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.191
And there were two great stories
this year.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
You mention the men
need a shot in the arm.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:08.528 size:84% position:42% line:92%
What do you think it is

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:10.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's lacking right now
for the men's game?

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:12.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I think that our best
athletes have a tendency

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:15.702
to play American football
and basketball, obviously.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.871 size:78% position:39%
So we have -- we need
to do a better job

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
giving more kids
the opportunity to play.

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:20.507 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's too expensive.

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:22.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I have a tennis
academy at Randall's Island.

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:24.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
I try to raise money
with the charity.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:26.012 line:92%
Get as many kids as possible

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's got to be
a cool factor, too.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we had that a bit
in the '70s and '80s

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I was playing,
not just because I was playing

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:34.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well,
but let's be honest, yeah.

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:35.321 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, one thing we were
talking about earlier today,

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.325 size:84% position:42%
knowing you were coming
on the show, you know,

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:42.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like the prime
of a tennis player in the '70s

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
was a lot shorter
than it is now.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.365 line:92%
You know, it just seems like

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:46.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
the way health
and fitness has changed,

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:49.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
the way even the equipment
has changed.

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:51.104 line:92%
For a shorter period of time

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:53.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
that guys in the '70s
were playing,

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
you had such a huge impact
on the game.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I do feel like
there was a huge cool factor

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.445
to what you were all doing
-I think we were the doing -

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:00.446 line:92%
the problem we were doing --

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were performance
detracting drugs.

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:04.584 line:92%
-Yeah, yeah, performance -

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.986
Yeah, nothing you were doing
made you better at tennis.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We tried to burn a candle
at both ends.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
it works for a while.

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:11.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it catches up to you
a little sooner.

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:13.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
These guys are incredible.
They got great teams.

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:16.930
People understand how to recover
quicker, et cetera.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that was a great time
in tennis.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:19.566 line:92%
There was a lot of personality

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:20.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
You need that
in a one-on-one sport.

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:23.970
That's why people gravitat
toward this Medvedev guy.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-He embraced being the bad guy

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is something
that I sort of wish

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
Djokovic would do
a little bit more of,

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
play the villain.
We need a villain.

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:33.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know nothing
about being a villain.

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:35.949 size:75% position:38% line:92%
But, you know, he --

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:38.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
and people, the fans
got behind him at the end.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- Of course you were -
You were literally --

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:43.957
the fact that you were known for
a little bit of bad behavior

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:45.124 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Was it ever --

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:47.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Just a little bit.

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:49.229 line:92%
-Was it genuinely that you wer

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:50.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
losing a temper
you couldn't control?

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or was there some
gamesmanship to it?

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:55.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it a strategy to get
in the head of your opponent

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:58.304 size:78% position:39%
by losing your temper
with, say, the judge?

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.907
-Well, if all it takes to ge
in the head of an opponent

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:04.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
is you getting -- telling
a judge that he sucks, okay.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:04.510 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.313
-What are the odds of the umpire
giving me the next call?

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, if you tell this guy
he's a bum, you know,

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:11.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
the next -- he's going to go
"I'll show that McEnroe."

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:14.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, to me, that was sour grape
if that's all it took.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, right.
-With all that goes on --

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:18.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, say in a football game
on Sunday, you think

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:20.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're saying, "Hello.
How are you?" on the field

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or basketball?
There's a lot of trash-talking

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:23.796 line:92%
We used to do more of that

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:27.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd like to see a little bit
more in the tennis.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:27.734 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So there was
genuine trash talk.

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:33.840
Of course, one of your rivals --
Bjorn Borg, there you are there.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:37.176
And he is genuinely
a dear friend of yours now, yes?

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:39.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I love him.
Hopefully, he loves me.

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:41.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's probably --
He's probably the only guy

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.216
that I didn't have problems with
on the court.

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:45.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, so you never
had an issue with him?

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:45.685 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-We never had a problem.

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:49.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
He took me, you know,
under his wing, in a way.

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I got respect
because of that.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause he was already,
like, a god.

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:54.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, he was like Federe
at the time.

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:55.094 line:92%
You know, everyone loved him

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:57.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was this
great-looking guy.

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:59.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dressed right.
The girls loved him.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I was like,
"I want to be like him."

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:02.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And he was the only guy
who was nice to you.

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:06.005
Do you feel like that means he
was a good judge of characte

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:07.607 size:75% position:38% line:92%
or just a bad judge?

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:08.308 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Was it a blind spot

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:10.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he was like,
"I like this McEnroe kid"?

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:11.811 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-What do you think?

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:12.378 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:14.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, the first time
you go to Wimbledon, is it -

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:15.682 line:92%
Are you 17 years old? Are you --

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:17.350
-I was 18 the first time I went.
-18 years old.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:20.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you talked about
how guys have great teams now.

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:22.422
And there's -- You know,
nutrition has, obviously,

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:24.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
advanced so much.
But what was it like --

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:28.494
The tour did not take care
of you in the same way the

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:29.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
as it does now.
-No.

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:32.498
-You know, it was an incredibl
time in England in the '70s.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.567 line:92%
You know, punk was breaking out.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:35.835 line:92%
People were getting on me.

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it was like
oil and water.

00:05:37.704 --> 00:05:38.404 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Me, a New York kid.

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:40.840
I mean, you're screaming
and yelling all the time.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:44.344
People are, you know -- They
give you their opinion, right?

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:46.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
Over there,
they're much more reserved

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:47.280 line:92%
They're very proper. I was like,

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What's wrong
with these people?"

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:49.449 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:51.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"You know, they're so
well behaved here."

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:53.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, you know,
we clashed right away.

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:55.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I got a lot of support
I got to say, like,

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:57.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you walked down
the equivalent of,

00:05:57.256 --> 00:06:00.126
well, I don't know what street
you can -- Kings Road in London.

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:02.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
It would be Lexington.
I don't know.

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:04.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And they got a lot of support

00:06:04.097 --> 00:06:06.866 size:78% position:39%
There was, like, some
freaky people around.

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:08.301 line:92%
But they were supportive.

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:10.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
The establishment
and the papers,

00:06:10.103 --> 00:06:11.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
which were owned
by Rupert Murdoch --

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:13.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
You may know him --
-Yeah.

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:15.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They were giving me
a very hard time.

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:18.478 size:81% position:41%
And there's a lot more
newspapers in London

00:06:18.478 --> 00:06:19.445 size:75% position:38% line:92%
than there are here.

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:20.646 line:92%
There was 15 local papers.

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:22.882 size:88% position:44%
So that makes it where
they looking to get you.

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:23.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you --
Were you somebody that --

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:26.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, you're 18 years old.
And you were supposed to -

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:28.688 line:92%
Your first run to, I think

00:06:28.688 --> 00:06:29.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
the semifinals?
-Semifinals.

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:30.890 size:75% position:38%
-So that was kind of
unexpected, right?

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:33.659
You were actually supposed to be
there to play in the juniors

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:35.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
You end going on
a sort of unexpected run.

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:37.697
Were you somebody then
who would read the paper?

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:39.565
I mean, you're in London
having this incredible run

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.467 size:81% position:41%
You're 18 years old.
-Initially, I read it.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:42.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought it was
the funniest thing ever.

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:44.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought,
"These people don't get it

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:46.806 size:81% position:41%
What's their problem?
I'm the one out there.

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:49.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, how -- Why are the
reacting this way?"

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:51.444 size:81% position:41%
But when I came home,
and everyone was like,

